Error [jet.ReturnTypeMismatch]: `label` and `numeric` disagree about `PORT`: This value is Int (a whole number), but `label` returns String
  --> tests/ui/module_value_consumers_disagree.jet:10:1
    |
 10 | PORT: port_for("https")
    | ^^^^
  --> tests/ui/module_value_consumers_disagree.jet:21:25
    |
 21 | label: fn() -> String { PORT }
    |                         ^^^^ `label` reads `PORT` here
  --> tests/ui/module_value_consumers_disagree.jet:19:24
    |
 19 | numeric: fn() -> Int { PORT + 1 }
    |                        ^^^^ `numeric` reads it here as Int (a whole number)
 Why: `label` declares String as its result, so the value it hands back must be String
 Fix: Put the value in text with interpolation: "{value}"
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0113

Error [jet.UnknownField]: `scheme_of` and `host_of` disagree about `ENDPOINT`: `Endpoint` has no field `scheme`
  --> tests/ui/module_value_consumers_disagree.jet:17:1
    |
 17 | ENDPOINT: Endpoint{host: "example.com", port: 8080}
    | ^^^^^^^^
  --> tests/ui/module_value_consumers_disagree.jet:25:29
    |
 25 | scheme_of: fn() -> String { ENDPOINT.scheme }
    |                             ^^^^^^^^ `scheme_of` reads `ENDPOINT` here
  --> tests/ui/module_value_consumers_disagree.jet:23:27
    |
 23 | host_of: fn() -> String { ENDPOINT.host }
    |                           ^^^^^^^^ `host_of` reads it here as `Endpoint`
 Why: Field access only works on names declared in the struct
 Fix: Check the field names on `Endpoint`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0302
